# Right-click equips; the equip hotkey runs the Lua move events (server/README.md "Right-click equips"). Owner request:
# "Make items get equipped on right-click."
#   * Game::chaosUseEquip, called by Actions::internalUseItem when an item has no action (before the stock
#     RETURNVALUE_CANNOTUSETHISOBJECT): a use of a piece of equipment the player carries in a container puts it on, a
#     use of a worn one takes it off into the backpack. The use is what the client's mouse controls send (a right-click
#     in the classic controls, Ctrl + click in the regular ones, a left-click in the smart ones, "Use" in the context
#     menu), so the controls keep their meanings and the exact item clicked moves (the equip hotkey packet names an
#     item type only and takes the first one found). Equipment: a head, necklace, armour, legs, feet or ring item, or a
#     sword, club, axe, distance weapon, wand, shield or quiver (every item may be held in a hand by default, so the
#     hands count by weapon type). Not: an item with an action (a scripted action that returns false still ends as
#     before), a container, ammunition, the base's extra slots (deck, badge, ship, belt, gloves), an item on the
#     ground, in a depot or someone else's, a hotkey use, an item that cannot be moved, and a player who turned it off
#     (player storage 7101810 = 1, written by data/scripts/chaos/rightclick_equip.lua from the client option "Right-click
#     equips items"). The slot is the equip hotkey's (getSlotType); a ring goes into the free ring slot (9 first), else
#     into the slot of a might ring when it is one (one might ring at a time, 0023), else into slot 9 (the rings swap).
#   * Game::playerUseItem: a multi-use item (the stock weapons are: their action is "break furniture", a use with) was
#     never used plainly. A plain use of one the player carries now goes to chaosUseEquip (not a hotkey use; its
#     action is a use with and is not run). The client sends that for the multi-use weapons the server lists
#     (data/scripts/chaos/rightclick_equip.lua: not the tools with a use with of their own, such as the machete);
#     every other click on them still starts the use with.
#   * Game::chaosEquipMove: the equip hotkey (Game::playerEquipItem) and a use that equips move the item with the
#     player as the actor and the client positions (an inventory slot {0xFFFF, slot, 0}, a container slot
#     {0xFFFF, 0x40 | cid, index}; a container the player has not open: cid 0x3F), so Player:onMoveItem and the
#     onMoveItem / onItemMoved callbacks run as for drag and drop. Before, the hotkey moved without them: the base
#     rarity script never saw the item (a club ring put on by hotkey gave its own +4 club, not the +9 with its rarity;
#     a worn item it swapped out kept its rarity conditions while the slot was taken), and neither did the item
#     modifiers, archery or default_onMoveItem.lua's two-handed swap (a two-handed weapon by hotkey next to a shield
#     was refused). Every refusal of the hotkey now shows its message (before: only the might ring's).
#   * Game::chaosTakeOff: a worn item goes into the backpack first, then wherever the stock hotkey put it
#     (Player::queryDestination) when the backpack has no room.
# Apply in the server source root after 0001-0023: patch -p1 < 0024-equip-on-use.patch, then rebuild.
